    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented idempotent create for `POST /api/owners`: when the request carries an `Idempotency-Key` header already seen, the endpoint returns the originally created owner with **200** instead of creating a duplicate (which would otherwise 409).\n\nThe change is purely additive \u2014 no existing function was modified, so no surrounding class complexity was inherited:\n\n**New function classes** (each one tiny method, `WMC_other = 0`):\n- `IdempotencyStore` \u2014 static key\u2192owner-id map plus a `keyOf(connection)` header reader.\n- `CheckIdempotentCreate` \u2014 new first pipeline step; throws `IdempotentCreateException` when the key was already used.\n- `RecordIdempotentCreate` \u2014 new step after `save`; records key\u2192new owner id.\n\n**New escalation** (mirrors the existing reject/handler pattern):\n- `IdempotentCreateException` (checked) + `IdempotentCreateExceptionHandler` \u2014 loads the original owner and sends it with 200.\n- `officefloor/escalation/...IdempotentCreateException.yml`.\n\n**Wiring:** `owners.POST.yml` gained a `checkIdempotency` step before `build` and a `recordIdempotency` step between `save` and `respond`.\n\nNotes:\n- I first tried Spring's `@RequestHeader(required=false)`, but in this OfficeFloor/Spring integration it didn't resolve the header, so I read it via the injected `ServerHttpConnection` (null-safe when absent, so ordinary keyless creates are unaffected).\n- The store is keyed by header value and skips null keys, so non-idempotent requests flow through the normal pipeline untouched.",
