    "probe_text": "Here's the complete ordered trace for `POST /api/owners`, as the code actually stands. The handler is the OfficeFloor pipeline in `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` (the `api/` directory supplies the base path). No legacy Spring `@RestController` for creating owners exists \u2014 the pipeline is the sole handler.\n\n## Before any step runs\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition: authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"` guards the file. Denial \u2192 **403** via `ForbiddenExceptionHandler`.\n- **Transaction governance** \u2014 every step from `build` onward has `govern: [ transaction ]`; the whole build\u2192respond pipeline commits once at the end. (`checkIdempotency` is outside it.)\n\n## Ordered validations & side-effects\n\n1. **`CheckIdempotentCreate`** \u2014 reads `Idempotency-Key` header; if that key already created an owner, throws `IdempotentCreateException` \u2192 **200**, returns the existing owner (short-circuits the create).\n2. **`BuildOwner`** \u2014 binds body with `@RequestBody` **without `@Valid`** (so the JSR-380 constraints on `OwnerFieldsDto` are *not* enforced). Manual required-field checks: `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`, and at least one of `addressLine1`/`address`; missing \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` \u2192 **400** `{errors:[...]}`. **Side-effect (mutation):** maps DTO\u2192`Owner` and sets `registrationDate` to `BusinessDay.nextBusinessDay(...)` (defaults to today if absent, then rolls weekends/2026 holidays forward).\n3. **`RejectFutureRegistrationDate`** \u2014 rejects a (rolled) registration date after today's rolled next-business-day \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` \u2192 **400**.\n4. **`ValidateOwnerPostcode`** \u2014 if postcode present: must match `[0-9]{4}`, and if the city maps to a known region must fall in NSW 2000\u20132099 / VIC 3000\u20133099 / QLD 4000\u20134099; invalid \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException(\"postcode\")` \u2192 **400**.\n5. **`NormalizeOwnerAddress`** \u2014 *mutation:* trims/collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE, composes `address`; blank after normalization \u2192 **400**.\n6. **`NormalizeOwnerTelephone`** \u2014 *mutation:* converts to E.164 (`+61` default, drops leading `0`, length checks); null result \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException(\"telephone\")` \u2192 **400**.\n7. **`NormalizeOwnerEmail`** \u2014 if present: must match email regex (else **400**); *mutation:* lower-cases; rejects disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 **400**.\n8. **`RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity`** \u2014 *repo read* (`findAll`); another non-deleted owner with same E.164 telephone **and** lower-cased email \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` \u2192 **409**.\n9. **`RejectDuplicateOwnerHousehold`** \u2014 if `sharesHousehold != true`: another non-deleted owner sharing the `HouseholdId` (SHA-256 of lastName + postcode) \u2192 **409**.\n10. **`RejectOwnerCityAtCapacity`** \u2014 *repo read;* \u2265 50 existing owners in the same city \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409**.\n11. **`RejectOwnerDailyLimit`** \u2014 *repo read;* \u2265 100 existing owners with the same registrationDate \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` \u2192 **429**.\n12. **`AssignOwnerCustomerCode`** \u2014 *mutation:* sets `customerCode = <REGION>-<HASH8>` (SHA-256 over telephone + lastName).\n13. **`DeduplicateOwnerCustomerCode`** \u2014 *repo read + mutation:* if the code collides, appends `-<n>` (smallest n \u2265 2).\n14. **`SaveOwner`** \u2014 **the persistence write:** `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (assigns id). Side-effects: computes namesake count / membership level / membership number and writes an **AUDIT log** line.\n15. **`RecordIdempotentCreate`** \u2014 *side-effect:* records new id under the `Idempotency-Key` (no-op if header absent) for future repeats.\n16. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto`, enriches (namesakeCount, membershipPoints/level, bulkSignupWarning, possibleDuplicate flags), responds **201 CREATED** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n- **The DTO's declared bean-validation is dead for create.** `OwnerFieldsDto` carries `@NotNull`/`@Pattern`/`@Size` on firstName, lastName, city, telephone, postcode, etc., but `BuildOwner` binds with `@RequestBody` **without `@Valid`**, so none of those constraints fire \u2014 all enforcement is the manual/normalization logic in steps 2\u20137.\n- **Persistence happens exactly once** (step 14), inside the single pipeline-wide transaction spanning steps 2\u201316, committed after the response is composed."
